Score the pairing video

An original arrangement rather than a licensed track, so the video carries no
rights but ours, and so it can be cut to the picture: at 112 BPM a bar line
lands within ~0.1s of four of the five scene cuts, the drums drop out through
the bar where the two codes are being compared, and the chord resolves on the
frame the link turns green. Three interface sounds sit on the frames they
belong to — a tick per machine the tailnet turns up, a press on Pair and on
Allow, and a rising fifth on paired, which is the same resolution the score
arrives at.

tools/make-audio.mjs synthesises all of it and is deterministic, so a re-run
rewrites the same bytes. The arrangement is one row per bar in PLAN, where
`level` scales the whole bar: the per-voice gains alone measured almost flat,
because a pad-only opening is within a couple of dB of the full band and the
limiter then flattened what was left. Softened knee, quieter hats and a 14kHz
master trim keep it a bed rather than a beat.

Mixed peak is -1.4dB with no clipping, and each sound measures 8 to 10dB over
the score at its own frame.
